description:
## Context

This is the **core component** that renders Stripe's ExpressCheckoutElement. It handles all payment button display (Apple Pay, Google Pay, Link, PayPal, Klarna) and user interactions. This component must be a client component (uses React hooks) and must be rendered within a Stripe Elements provider context.

**Blocked by:** EXP-001 (Domain Registration), EXP-002 (Payment Methods Enabled)

---

## File to Create

```
table-clay-storefront/src/modules/checkout/components/express-checkout/express-checkout-button.tsx
```

---

## Current Architecture Reference

### Existing Stripe Integration
- **Stripe packages**: `@stripe/react-stripe-js` v5.3.0, `@stripe/stripe-js` v8.2.0
- **Elements Provider**: `src/modules/checkout/components/payment-wrapper/stripe-wrapper.tsx`
- **Payment Button**: `src/modules/checkout/components/payment-button/index.tsx` (uses confirmCardPayment)
- **Cart Actions**: `src/lib/data/cart.ts` (initiatePaymentSession, placeOrder, updateCart)

### Payment Session Flow
1. Cart created with items
2. `initiatePaymentSession()` creates PaymentIntent, returns `client_secret`
3. `client_secret` stored in `cart.payment_collection.payment_sessions[].data.client_secret`
4. Express Checkout uses same `client_secret` for `stripe.confirmPayment()`
5. On success, `placeOrder()` completes the order in Medusa

---

## Full Implementation

```typescript
"use client"

import {
  ExpressCheckoutElement,
  useStripe,
  useElements,
} from "@stripe/react-stripe-js"
import {
  StripeExpressCheckoutElementClickEvent,
  StripeExpressCheckoutElementConfirmEvent,
  StripeExpressCheckoutElementReadyEvent,
  StripeExpressCheckoutElementOptions,
} from "@stripe/stripe-js"
import { useState, useCallback } from "react"
import { HttpTypes } from "@medusajs/types"
import { placeOrder } from "@lib/data/cart"

interface ExpressCheckoutButtonProps {
  cart: HttpTypes.StoreCart
  notReady?: boolean
}

// Map Stripe address format to Medusa address format
const mapStripeAddressToMedusa = (
  stripeAddress: any,
  name?: string
): Partial<HttpTypes.StoreCartAddress> | undefined => {
  if (!stripeAddress) return undefined

  const nameParts = name?.split(" ") || []
  const firstName = nameParts[0] || ""
  const lastName = nameParts.slice(1).join(" ") || ""

  return {
    first_name: firstName,
    last_name: lastName,
    address_1: stripeAddress.line1 || "",
    address_2: stripeAddress.line2 || "",
    city: stripeAddress.city || "",
    province: stripeAddress.state || "",
    postal_code: stripeAddress.postal_code || "",
    country_code: stripeAddress.country?.toLowerCase() || "",
  }
}

const ExpressCheckoutButton: React.FC<ExpressCheckoutButtonProps> = ({
  cart,
  notReady,
}) => {
  const stripe = useStripe()
  const elements = useElements()

  const [isAvailable, setIsAvailable] = useState(false)
  const [errorMessage, setErrorMessage] = useState<string | null>(null)
  const [isProcessing, setIsProcessing] = useState(false)

  // Get client_secret from payment session
  const paymentSession = cart.payment_collection?.payment_sessions?.find(
    (s) => s.status === "pending"
  )
  const clientSecret = paymentSession?.data?.client_secret as string | undefined

  // Called when Express Checkout Element is ready
  const onReady = useCallback(
    ({ availablePaymentMethods }: StripeExpressCheckoutElementReadyEvent) => {
      // Show component only if at least one express method is available
      const hasExpressMethods =
        availablePaymentMethods?.applePay ||
        availablePaymentMethods?.googlePay ||
        availablePaymentMethods?.link ||
        availablePaymentMethods?.paypal

      setIsAvailable(!!hasExpressMethods)
    },
    []
  )

  // Called when user clicks a payment button (before payment sheet opens)
  const onClick = useCallback(
    ({ resolve }: StripeExpressCheckoutElementClickEvent) => {
      // Configure the payment sheet
      const options = {
        emailRequired: !cart.email,
        phoneNumberRequired: false,
        // Only require shipping if not already set
        shippingAddressRequired: !cart.shipping_address?.address_1,
        // Allowed shipping countries
        allowedShippingCountries: cart.region?.countries?.map(
          (c) => c.iso_2?.toUpperCase()
        ) as any[] || ["US"],
        // Show line items in payment sheet
        lineItems: cart.items?.map((item) => ({
          name: item.product_title || item.title,
          amount: item.unit_price || 0,
        })),
      }

      resolve(options)
    },
    [cart]
  )

  // Called when user confirms payment in the payment sheet
  const onConfirm = useCallback(
    async (event: StripeExpressCheckoutElementConfirmEvent) => {
      if (!stripe || !elements || !clientSecret) {
        setErrorMessage("Payment system not ready. Please refresh and try again.")
        return
      }

      setIsProcessing(true)
      setErrorMessage(null)

      try {
        const { billingDetails, shippingAddress } = event

        // Confirm the payment with Stripe
        const { error, paymentIntent } = await stripe.confirmPayment({
          elements,
          clientSecret,
          confirmParams: {
            return_url: `${window.location.origin}/${cart.region?.countries?.[0]?.iso_2 || "us"}/order/confirmed`,
            payment_method_data: {
              billing_details: billingDetails,
            },
          },
          redirect: "if_required",
        })

        if (error) {
          setErrorMessage(error.message || "Payment failed. Please try again.")
          setIsProcessing(false)
          return
        }

        // Check payment status
        if (
          paymentIntent?.status === "succeeded" ||
          paymentIntent?.status === "requires_capture"
        ) {
          // Place the order in Medusa
          await placeOrder()
        } else {
          setErrorMessage("Payment was not completed. Please try again.")
        }
      } catch (err: any) {
        console.error("Express checkout error:", err)
        setErrorMessage(err.message || "An unexpected error occurred.")
      } finally {
        setIsProcessing(false)
      }
    },
    [stripe, elements, clientSecret, cart]
  )

  // Called when user cancels the payment sheet
  const onCancel = useCallback(() => {
    setErrorMessage(null)
    setIsProcessing(false)
  }, [])

  // Don't render if not ready, no client secret, or no express methods available
  if (notReady || !clientSecret || !isAvailable) {
    return null
  }

  const expressCheckoutOptions: StripeExpressCheckoutElementOptions = {
    buttonTheme: {
      applePay: "black",
      googlePay: "black",
      paypal: "gold",
    },
    buttonType: {
      applePay: "buy",
      googlePay: "buy",
      paypal: "checkout",
    },
    buttonHeight: 48,
    layout: {
      maxColumns: 3,
      maxRows: 1,
      overflow: "never",
    },
    paymentMethods: {
      applePay: "auto",
      googlePay: "auto",
      link: "auto",
      paypal: "auto",
    },
  }

  return (
    <div className="w-full">
      <ExpressCheckoutElement
        options={expressCheckoutOptions}
        onReady={onReady}
        onClick={onClick}
        onConfirm={onConfirm}
        onCancel={onCancel}
      />

      {errorMessage && (
        <p className="text-red-500 text-sm mt-2 text-center">{errorMessage}</p>
      )}

      {isProcessing && (
        <p className="text-ui-fg-muted text-sm mt-2 text-center">
          Processing payment...
        </p>
      )}
    </div>
  )
}

export default ExpressCheckoutButton
```

---

## Key Implementation Notes

1. **useStripe/useElements hooks** - Must be inside Elements provider
2. **availablePaymentMethods** - Object with boolean flags for each method (applePay, googlePay, link, paypal)
3. **clientSecret** - Required for confirmPayment, comes from payment session
4. **placeOrder()** - Existing server action that completes the order in Medusa
5. **redirect: "if_required"** - Prevents redirect for wallet payments that complete inline

---

## Dependencies

- Must be rendered within `<Elements>` provider with clientSecret
- Requires payment session to be initiated (has client_secret)
- Uses existing `placeOrder()` from `@lib/data/cart`

---

## Acceptance Criteria

- [ ] Component renders ExpressCheckoutElement
- [ ] Buttons appear based on device/browser capabilities
- [ ] onClick configures payment sheet with cart data
- [ ] onConfirm calls stripe.confirmPayment then placeOrder
- [ ] Error messages display to user
- [ ] Loading state shown during processing
- [ ] Component hidden when no express methods available

---

## Testing Notes

- Apple Pay only shows on Safari (macOS/iOS) on registered domains
- Google Pay shows on Chrome
- Link shows when user has a Stripe Link account
- PayPal redirects to PayPal for auth

## Context
**SIMPLIFIED**: Admin-curated review/testimonial system. No customer submission, no moderation workflow, no voting. Admin has full control over all review content including stats display.

**Reference Images:**
- `Reference_Images/Product_Page/Review_Module.png` - Review display with stats header
- `Reference_Images/Product_Page/Review_Module_Continued.png` - Individual review cards
- `Reference_Images/Product_Page/Review_Module_con.png` - Additional review examples

## Key Decisions (from requirements interview)

| Decision | Choice |
|----------|--------|
| Review source | Admin-curated only (no customer submission) |
| Review stats | Admin manually sets average rating + count |
| Verified buyer | Admin-controlled checkbox (not auto-detected) |
| Review images | Admin uploads to S3 |
| Display date | Admin sets custom display date |
| Photo viewing | Inline only (no lightbox) |
| Replies | Not supported (simpler system) |
| Voting | Not supported (admin controls helpful count) |

## Data Model

### Review Model (in Content Module)
This model will be part of the combined Content Module (Reviews + FAQ).

```typescript
import { model } from '@medusajs/framework/utils'

export const Review = model.define('review', {
  id: model.id().primaryKey(),
  product_id: model.text(),              // Links to Medusa product

  // Customer info (admin-entered)
  customer_name: model.text(),           // 'Emma T.'
  is_verified_buyer: model.boolean().default(false),  // Admin checkbox

  // Review content
  rating: model.number(),                // 1-5 stars
  title: model.text().nullable(),        // 'My new favorite hobby!'
  content: model.text(),                 // Full review text

  // Display settings
  display_date: model.dateTime(),        // Admin-set date shown to customers
  helpful_count: model.number().default(0),  // Admin-set number

  is_active: model.boolean().default(true),
  sort_order: model.number().default(0),
  metadata: model.json().nullable(),
})
.indexes([
  { on: ['product_id', 'is_active'], name: 'idx_review_product_active' },
])
```

