## Key Differences from Checkout Express Checkout

| Aspect | Checkout Page | Product Page |
|--------|--------------|--------------|
| Cart | Already exists | Created on-the-fly |
| Payment Session | Already initiated | Initiated when variant selected |
| Elements Provider | Uses existing wrapper | Creates its own |
| Shipping | May already be set | Always collected in sheet |

---

## Flow Diagram

```
1. User lands on product page
2. User selects variant (size, color, etc.)
3. useEffect triggers:
   a. addToCart() - adds variant to cart
   b. retrieveCart() - gets cart ID
   c. initiatePaymentSession() - creates PaymentIntent
4. clientSecret received → ExpressCheckoutElement renders
5. User clicks Apple Pay/Google Pay
6. Payment sheet opens:
   a. User enters/selects shipping address
   b. Shipping rates fetched from Medusa
   c. User selects shipping rate
   d. User confirms payment
7. onConfirm:
   a. stripe.confirmPayment()
   b. placeOrder(cartId)
8. Redirect to order confirmation
```

---

## Important Notes

- Creates its own Elements provider (separate from checkout page)
- Pre-creates cart and payment session when variant is selected
- Handles full checkout flow within Express Checkout payment sheet
- Self-contained component - no dependencies on checkout page components

